IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ita-amounts`
IMPORT `ita-individual`

-- Income Tax Act -- worked cases on the seat-neutral core (ita-individual.l4), the 2026 taxation year and the benefit
-- months that follow it.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked against
-- CRA forms, the T1 return, the CRA's calculators or any ruling. Expected values were worked by hand from the deposited
-- text and the CRA's 2026 indexation table; the arithmetic is shown in the comment above each case. Amounts are not
-- rounded to cents: the Act computes in dollars, and the forms' rounding is not deposited.
--
-- The CPP contributions, EI premiums and OAS pension amounts in these cases are inputs chosen for the case. They are not
-- worked out from the Canada Pension Plan, Employment Insurance Act or Old Age Security Act, whose encodings (another
-- agent) compute them.
--
-- The three cases the brief asks for: an employee (Priya), a single parent of two on the CCB and the CWB (Jordan), and a
-- pensioner with OAS who pays the recovery tax (Margaret). The others test one rule each.

§ `Fixtures`

GIVEN emp IS A NUMBER, s8 IS A NUMBER, oas IS A NUMBER, gis IS A NUMBER, cpp IS A NUMBER, ann IS A NUMBER, oth IS A NUMBER, ei IS A NUMBER, sa IS A NUMBER, prop IS A NUMBER, bus IS A NUMBER, rrsp IS A NUMBER, lim IS A NUMBER, enh IS A NUMBER, base IS A NUMBER, eip IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `Income amounts`
`income of employment` emp `less s 8` s8 `OAS` oas `GIS` gis `CPP` cpp `annuity` ann `other pension` oth `EI` ei `social assistance` sa `property` prop `business` bus `RRSP` rrsp `limit` lim `enhanced CPP` enh `base CPP` base `EI premiums` eip MEANS `Income amounts` WITH
    `employment income`                               IS emp
    `deductions under s 8`                            IS s8
    `OAS pension`                                     IS oas
    `OAS supplement or allowance`                     IS gis
    `CPP or QPP benefits`                             IS cpp
    `life annuity payments from a pension plan`       IS ann
    `other pension income listed in s 118(7)`         IS oth
    `of which received because of a spouse's death`   IS 0
    `EI benefits`                                     IS ei
    `social assistance`                               IS sa
    `property income`                                 IS prop
    `business income or loss`                         IS bus
    `other income`                                    IS 0
    `taxable capital gains`                           IS 0
    `RRSP premiums paid for the year`                 IS rrsp
    `RRSP deduction limit`                            IS lim
    `enhanced CPP contributions`                      IS enh
    `base CPP contributions`                          IS base
    `EI premiums`                                     IS eip

`resident all year` MEANS `Residence facts` WITH
    `resident in Canada throughout the year`          IS TRUE
    `resident in Canada for part of the year only`    IS FALSE
    `days sojourned in Canada in the year`            IS 365
    `deemed resident under s 250(1)(b) to (g)`        IS FALSE

`no spouse` MEANS `Spouse facts` WITH
    `married or in a common-law partnership in the year` IS FALSE
    `supports the spouse`                             IS FALSE
    `living separate and apart because of a breakdown` IS FALSE
    `a cohabiting spouse at the end of the year`      IS FALSE
    `the spouse's income`                             IS 0
    `the spouse is dependent on the individual by reason of infirmity` IS FALSE
    `the spouse was resident in Canada throughout the year` IS FALSE
    `the spouse is an ineligible individual under s 122.7(1)` IS FALSE
    `the spouse's working income`                     IS 0
    `the spouse may deduct a disability amount under s 118.3(1)` IS FALSE

-- A cohabiting spouse, supported, resident all year, with the given income (all of it working income) and DTC status.
GIVEN inc IS A NUMBER, dtc IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Spouse facts`
`a spouse with income` inc `DTC` dtc MEANS `Spouse facts` WITH
    `married or in a common-law partnership in the year` IS TRUE
    `supports the spouse`                             IS TRUE
    `living separate and apart because of a breakdown` IS FALSE
    `a cohabiting spouse at the end of the year`      IS TRUE
    `the spouse's income`                             IS inc
    `the spouse is dependent on the individual by reason of infirmity` IS FALSE
    `the spouse was resident in Canada throughout the year` IS TRUE
    `the spouse is an ineligible individual under s 122.7(1)` IS FALSE
    `the spouse's working income`                     IS inc
    `the spouse may deduct a disability amount under s 118.3(1)` IS dtc

`no eligible dependant` MEANS `Eligible dependant facts` WITH
    `claimed`                                         IS FALSE
    `maintains a self-contained domestic establishment and supports the person in it` IS FALSE
    `wholly dependent for support on the individual`  IS FALSE
    `related to the individual`                       IS FALSE
    `a child of the individual`                       IS FALSE
    `resident in Canada`                              IS FALSE
    `a parent or grandparent of the individual`       IS FALSE
    `age at the end of the year`                      IS 0
    `dependent by reason of mental or physical infirmity` IS FALSE
    `income for the year`                             IS 0
    `s 118(5) excludes the claim`                     IS FALSE

-- A child of the individual, living in the individual's home, wholly dependent, with no income.
GIVEN age IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `Eligible dependant facts`
`my child aged` age MEANS `Eligible dependant facts` WITH
    `claimed`                                         IS TRUE
    `maintains a self-contained domestic establishment and supports the person in it` IS TRUE
    `wholly dependent for support on the individual`  IS TRUE
    `related to the individual`                       IS TRUE
    `a child of the individual`                       IS TRUE
    `resident in Canada`                              IS TRUE
    `a parent or grandparent of the individual`       IS FALSE
    `age at the end of the year`                      IS age
    `dependent by reason of mental or physical infirmity` IS FALSE
    `income for the year`                             IS 0
    `s 118(5) excludes the claim`                     IS FALSE

`no disability` MEANS `Disability facts` WITH
    `a certified disability tax credit certificate is filed for the year` IS FALSE
    `attendant care or nursing home costs are claimed under s 118.2` IS FALSE
    `care and supervision amounts claimed under ss 63, 64 and 118.2` IS 0

GIVEN care IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Disability facts`
`a disability certificate with care costs` care MEANS `Disability facts` WITH
    `a certified disability tax credit certificate is filed for the year` IS TRUE
    `attendant care or nursing home costs are claimed under s 118.2` IS FALSE
    `care and supervision amounts claimed under ss 63, 64 and 118.2` IS care

GIVEN y IS A NUMBER, prov IS A `Province at the end of the year`, age IS A NUMBER, inc IS AN `Income amounts`, sp IS A `Spouse facts`, ed IS AN `Eligible dependant facts`, d IS A `Disability facts`, wh IS A NUMBER, oaswh IS A NUMBER, inst IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Taxation year`
`the year` y `in` prov `aged` age `with` inc `spouse` sp `dependant` ed `disability` d `withheld` wh `OAS withheld` oaswh `instalments` inst MEANS `Taxation year` WITH
    `year`                                            IS y
    `residence`                                       IS `resident all year`
    `province at the end of the year`                 IS prov
    `died in the year`                                IS FALSE
    `age at the end of the year`                      IS age
    `income`                                          IS inc
    `spouse`                                          IS sp
    `eligible dependant`                              IS ed
    `disability`                                      IS d
    `income tax withheld at source`                   IS wh
    `Part I.2 tax withheld from OAS payments`         IS oaswh
    `instalments paid for the year`                   IS inst

-- CWB facts: files a return, not ineligible, the one who claims.
GIVEN parent IS A BOOLEAN, dep IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `CWB facts`
`CWB facts with a child at home` parent `and an eligible dependant` dep MEANS `CWB facts` WITH
    `the parent of a child with whom the individual resides` IS parent
    `has an eligible dependant`                       IS dep
    `described in s 149(1)(a) or (b)`                 IS FALSE
    `a full-time student for more than 13 weeks`      IS FALSE
    `confined to a prison for 90 days or more`        IS FALSE
    `the individual is the one of the couple who claims` IS TRUE
    `files a return of income for the year`           IS TRUE

`plain CWB facts` MEANS `CWB facts with a child at home` FALSE `and an eligible dependant` FALSE

-- The return's figures, or zeros where not covered (so a case can compare one figure).
GIVEN a IS AN `Answer` `Return figures`
GIVETH A `Return figures`
`figures of` a MEANS
    CONSIDER a
    WHEN `answered` f THEN f
    WHEN `not covered` r THEN `Return figures` WITH
        `income` IS 0
        `taxable income` IS 0
        `tax at the s 117(2) rates` IS 0
        `non-refundable credits` IS 0
        `Part I tax payable` IS 0
        `Part I.2 OAS recovery tax` IS 0
        `Canada workers benefit` IS 0
        `balance owing` IS 0

`the 2026 amounts` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the indexed amounts for the taxation year` 2026
    WHEN JUST ia THEN ia
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the 2026 amounts`

§ `Case 1: Priya, an employee in Ontario`

-- Priya, 34, single, no children, resident in Ontario all of 2026. Salary $72,000; union dues $600 (s 8(1)(i)); RRSP
-- premiums $5,000 with a deduction limit of $12,000; base CPP contributions $3,500, enhanced CPP contributions $800, EI
-- premiums $1,100 (inputs); $9,000 withheld.
--   s 3: 72,000 - 600 = 71,400; subdivision e: RRSP 5,000 (s 146(5), lesser of 5,000 and 12,000) + s 60(e.1) 800 = 5,800;
--   income 65,600. No OAS, so no Part I.2 tax. Taxable income 65,600.
--   s 117(2): 14% x 58,523 = 8,193.22; 20.5% x (65,600 - 58,523 = 7,077) = 1,450.785; total 9,644.005.
--   Credits: basic personal amount 16,452 (income under 181,440, E nil) under s 118(1)(c); Canada employment amount 1,501;
--   s 118.7: 1,100 + 3,500 = 4,600. Total 22,553 x 14% = 3,157.42. Top-up: 3,157.42 is under 14% x 58,523, so nil.
--   Part I tax 9,644.005 - 3,157.42 = 6,486.585. CWB: B = 15% x (65,600 - 27,392) exceeds A, nil.
--   Balance 6,486.585 - 9,000 = -2,513.415 (an overpayment).
`Priya's income` MEANS `income of employment` 72000 `less s 8` 600 `OAS` 0 `GIS` 0 `CPP` 0 `annuity` 0 `other pension` 0 `EI` 0 `social assistance` 0 `property` 0 `business` 0 `RRSP` 5000 `limit` 12000 `enhanced CPP` 800 `base CPP` 3500 `EI premiums` 1100
`Priya` MEANS `the year` 2026 `in` `another province or territory` `aged` 34 `with` `Priya's income` `spouse` `no spouse` `dependant` `no eligible dependant` `disability` `no disability` `withheld` 9000 `OAS withheld` 0 `instalments` 0
`Priya's return` MEANS `figures of` (`the return for the year` `Priya` `plain CWB facts`)

#ASSERT `the gap in` `Priya` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Priya's return`'s `income` EQUALS 65600
#ASSERT `Priya's return`'s `taxable income` EQUALS 65600
#ASSERT `Priya's return`'s `tax at the s 117(2) rates` EQUALS 9644.005
#ASSERT `Priya's return`'s `non-refundable credits` EQUALS 3157.42
#ASSERT `Priya's return`'s `Part I tax payable` EQUALS 6486.585
#ASSERT `Priya's return`'s `Part I.2 OAS recovery tax` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `Priya's return`'s `Canada workers benefit` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `Priya's return`'s `balance owing` EQUALS -2513.415
#ASSERT `the status under s 118(1)` `no spouse` `no eligible dependant` EQUALS `paragraph (c), single status`
-- She must file (Part I tax payable), by 30 April 2027, day 120.
#ASSERT `a return is required` 6486.585 0 (`Filing facts` WITH `had a taxable capital gain or disposed of capital property` IS FALSE, `has a positive HBP or LLP balance at the end of the year` IS FALSE, `the Minister has demanded a return` IS FALSE, `the individual or the cohabiting spouse carried on a business` IS FALSE, `able to file` IS TRUE)

§ `Case 2: Jordan, a single parent of two in British Columbia, on the CCB and the CWB`

-- Jordan, 31, not married, lives in British Columbia with two children: Sam, 4, and Alex, 8 at the end of 2026 (3 and 7
-- at the beginning of July 2026... taken here as 4 and 7). Wages $28,000; base CPP $1,300, enhanced CPP $250, EI premiums
-- $460 (inputs); $1,200 withheld. Jordan claims the s 118(1)(b) amount for Alex.
--   Income 28,000 - 250 = 27,750; taxable income 27,750; s 117(2) tax 14% x 27,750 = 3,885.
--   Credits: s 118(1)(b): 16,452 + (0 + 16,452 - 0) = 32,904; Canada employment 1,501; s 118.7 460 + 1,300 = 1,760. Total
--   36,165 x 14% = 5,063.10. Part I tax: nil (the credits exceed the tax).
--   CWB (s 122.7(2)), with an eligible dependant: A = lesser of 2,869 and 27% x (28,000 - 3,000) = 6,750, so 2,869;
--   B = 15% x (27,750 - 31,251), nil. CWB 2,869. Balance: 0 - (1,200 + 2,869) = -4,069.
`Jordan's income` MEANS `income of employment` 28000 `less s 8` 0 `OAS` 0 `GIS` 0 `CPP` 0 `annuity` 0 `other pension` 0 `EI` 0 `social assistance` 0 `property` 0 `business` 0 `RRSP` 0 `limit` 0 `enhanced CPP` 250 `base CPP` 1300 `EI premiums` 460
`Jordan` MEANS `the year` 2026 `in` `another province or territory` `aged` 31 `with` `Jordan's income` `spouse` `no spouse` `dependant` (`my child aged` 8) `disability` `no disability` `withheld` 1200 `OAS withheld` 0 `instalments` 0
`Jordan's CWB facts` MEANS `CWB facts with a child at home` TRUE `and an eligible dependant` TRUE
`Jordan's return` MEANS `figures of` (`the return for the year` `Jordan` `Jordan's CWB facts`)

#ASSERT `Jordan's return`'s `income` EQUALS 27750
#ASSERT `Jordan's return`'s `tax at the s 117(2) rates` EQUALS 3885
#ASSERT `the status under s 118(1)` `no spouse` (`my child aged` 8) EQUALS `paragraph (b), wholly dependent person`
#ASSERT `Jordan's return`'s `non-refundable credits` EQUALS 5063.10
#ASSERT `Jordan's return`'s `Part I tax payable` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `Jordan's return`'s `Canada workers benefit` EQUALS 2869
#ASSERT `Jordan's return`'s `balance owing` EQUALS -4069
-- No Part I tax, no gain, no demand: s 150(1.1)(b) means Jordan is not required to file. The CWB, CCB and GST/HST credit
-- all need a return (NOTES.md finding 2).
#ASSERT NOT (`a return is required` 0 0 (`Filing facts` WITH `had a taxable capital gain or disposed of capital property` IS FALSE, `has a positive HBP or LLP balance at the end of the year` IS FALSE, `the Minister has demanded a return` IS FALSE, `the individual or the cohabiting spouse carried on a business` IS FALSE, `able to file` IS TRUE))

-- The CCB for July 2026 (base taxation year 2025). Jordan's 2025 adjusted income: $26,500, under the first threshold
-- of 38,237, so Q is nil. E = 8,157 (Sam, under six) + 6,883 (Alex) = 15,040. Monthly: 15,040 / 12.
GIVEN age IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `CCB child`
`a child living with me aged` age MEANS `CCB child` WITH
    `age at the beginning of the month`               IS age
    `resides with the individual`                     IS TRUE
    `the individual primarily fulfils the responsibility for care and upbringing` IS TRUE
    `the individual is a shared-custody parent`       IS FALSE
    `claimed as a spouse or under a special allowance` IS FALSE
    `the disability amount may be deducted for the child` IS FALSE
    `a notice has been filed for the child`           IS TRUE

GIVEN y IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, ai IS A NUMBER, kids IS A LIST OF `CCB child`
GIVETH A `CCB facts`
`CCB for` y m `adjusted income` ai `children` kids MEANS `CCB facts` WITH
    `year of the month`                               IS y
    `month`                                           IS m
    `children`                                        IS kids
    `resident in Canada`                              IS TRUE
    `described in s 149(1)(a) or (b)`                 IS FALSE
    `the individual or the spouse has a status in s 122.6 (e)` IS TRUE
    `returns filed for the base taxation year`        IS TRUE
    `adjusted income for the base taxation year`      IS ai

`Jordan's children` MEANS LIST (`a child living with me aged` 4), (`a child living with me aged` 7)

#ASSERT `the base taxation year for` 2026 7 EQUALS 2025
#ASSERT `the base taxation year for` 2027 3 EQUALS 2025
#ASSERT `the Canada child benefit for the month` (`CCB for` 2026 7 `adjusted income` 26500 `children` `Jordan's children`) EQUALS `answered` (15040 DIVIDED BY 12)
-- At $50,000 of adjusted income: Q = 13.5% x (50,000 - 38,237 = 11,763) = 1,588.005; A = 15,040 - 1,588.005 = 13,451.995.
#ASSERT `the Canada child benefit for the month` (`CCB for` 2026 7 `adjusted income` 50000 `children` `Jordan's children`) EQUALS `answered` (13451.995 DIVIDED BY 12)

-- The GST/HST credit for July 2026 (taxation year 2025, s 122.5(4.5)). No qualified relation; two qualified dependants;
-- the s 118(1)(b) amount claimed for one. A = 445 + 445 (c) + 234 x 1 (d) + 234 (e) = 1,358; B nil (26,500 is under
-- 46,432). A quarter: 339.50.
GIVEN y IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, age IS A NUMBER, qr IS A BOOLEAN, qd IS A NUMBER, claims IS A BOOLEAN, inc IS A NUMBER, ai IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `GST credit facts`
`GST credit for` y m `aged` age `qualified relation` qr `dependants` qd `claims s 118(1)(b)` claims `income` inc `adjusted income` ai MEANS `GST credit facts` WITH
    `year of the month`                               IS y
    `month`                                           IS m
    `age before the month`                            IS age
    `before the month, a parent who resided with their child` IS qd GREATER THAN 0
    `before the month, married or in a common-law partnership` IS qr
    `excluded by s 122.5(2)`                          IS FALSE
    `has a qualified relation`                        IS qr
    `the individual is the one designated for the couple` IS TRUE
    `number of qualified dependants`                  IS qd
    `a shared-custody parent of a qualified dependant` IS FALSE
    `claims the s 118(1)(b) amount for a qualified dependant` IS claims
    `files a return of income for the taxation year`  IS TRUE
    `income for the taxation year`                    IS inc
    `adjusted income for the taxation year`           IS ai

#ASSERT `the GST/HST credit for the specified month` (`GST credit for` 2026 7 `aged` 31 `qualified relation` FALSE `dependants` 2 `claims s 118(1)(b)` TRUE `income` 26500 `adjusted income` 26500) EQUALS `answered` 339.5
#ASSERT `the taxation year for the specified month` 2027 1 EQUALS 2025
#ASSERT `the taxation year for the specified month` 2027 10 EQUALS 2026

§ `Case 3: Margaret, a pensioner with OAS who pays the recovery tax`

-- Margaret, 72, widowed, lives in Nova Scotia. 2026: OAS pension $8,900 (input), CPP $13,000, a life annuity from her
-- registered pension plan $68,000, RRIF payments $15,000, interest $4,000. $17,000 withheld under s 153 and $1,200 of
-- Part I.2 tax withheld from her OAS.
--   s 3(a) total 108,900. Part I.2 adjusted income 108,900 (no s 60(w) deduction).
--   s 180.2(2): 15% x (108,900 - 95,323 = 13,577) = 2,036.55, under the OAS of 8,900; Part I.2 tax 2,036.55.
--   Income (after s 60(w)) 108,900 - 2,036.55 = 106,863.45 = taxable income.
--   s 117(2): 8,193.22 + 20.5% x (106,863.45 - 58,523 = 48,340.45) = 8,193.22 + 9,909.79225 = 18,103.01225.
--   Credits: basic personal amount 16,452; age amount 9,208 - 15% x (106,863.45 - 46,432 = 60,431.45) = 9,208 - 9,064.7175
--   = 143.2825; pension amount: lesser of 2,000 and 83,000 = 2,000. Total 18,595.2825 x 14% = 2,603.33955. Top-up nil.
--   Part I tax 18,103.01225 - 2,603.33955 = 15,499.6727.
--   Balance (15,499.6727 + 2,036.55) - (17,000 + 1,200) = -663.7773.
`Margaret's income` MEANS `income of employment` 0 `less s 8` 0 `OAS` 8900 `GIS` 0 `CPP` 13000 `annuity` 68000 `other pension` 15000 `EI` 0 `social assistance` 0 `property` 4000 `business` 0 `RRSP` 0 `limit` 0 `enhanced CPP` 0 `base CPP` 0 `EI premiums` 0
`Margaret` MEANS `the year` 2026 `in` `another province or territory` `aged` 72 `with` `Margaret's income` `spouse` `no spouse` `dependant` `no eligible dependant` `disability` `no disability` `withheld` 17000 `OAS withheld` 1200 `instalments` 0
`Margaret's return` MEANS `figures of` (`the return for the year` `Margaret` `plain CWB facts`)

#ASSERT `the Part I.2 adjusted income` `Margaret's income` EQUALS 108900
#ASSERT `Margaret's return`'s `Part I.2 OAS recovery tax` EQUALS 2036.55
#ASSERT `Margaret's return`'s `income` EQUALS 106863.45
#ASSERT `Margaret's return`'s `taxable income` EQUALS 106863.45
#ASSERT `Margaret's return`'s `tax at the s 117(2) rates` EQUALS 18103.01225
#ASSERT `the s 118(2) age amount` `the 2026 amounts` 72 106863.45 EQUALS 143.2825
#ASSERT `the s 118(3) pension amount` 72 `Margaret's income` EQUALS 2000
#ASSERT `Margaret's return`'s `non-refundable credits` EQUALS 2603.33955
#ASSERT `Margaret's return`'s `Part I tax payable` EQUALS 15499.6727
#ASSERT `Margaret's return`'s `balance owing` EQUALS -663.7773
#ASSERT `a return is required` 15499.6727 2036.55 (`Filing facts` WITH `had a taxable capital gain or disposed of capital property` IS FALSE, `has a positive HBP or LLP balance at the end of the year` IS FALSE, `the Minister has demanded a return` IS FALSE, `the individual or the cohabiting spouse carried on a business` IS FALSE, `able to file` IS TRUE)
-- With $200,000 of other income the recovery tax is the whole OAS: 15% x (208,900 - 95,323) = 17,036.55, capped at 8,900.
#ASSERT `the Part I.2 tax` `the 2026 amounts` (`income of employment` 0 `less s 8` 0 `OAS` 8900 `GIS` 0 `CPP` 0 `annuity` 200000 `other pension` 0 `EI` 0 `social assistance` 0 `property` 0 `business` 0 `RRSP` 0 `limit` 0 `enhanced CPP` 0 `base CPP` 0 `EI premiums` 0) EQUALS 8900

§ `One rule at a time`

-- Residence (s 250(1)(a)): 200 days' sojourn deems residence throughout the year; part-year residence is not covered.
#ASSERT `the residence status` (`Residence facts` WITH `resident in Canada throughout the year` IS FALSE, `resident in Canada for part of the year only` IS FALSE, `days sojourned in Canada in the year` IS 200, `deemed resident under s 250(1)(b) to (g)` IS FALSE) EQUALS `resident throughout the year`
#ASSERT `the residence status` (`Residence facts` WITH `resident in Canada throughout the year` IS FALSE, `resident in Canada for part of the year only` IS TRUE, `days sojourned in Canada in the year` IS 120, `deemed resident under s 250(1)(b) to (g)` IS FALSE) EQUALS `resident for part of the year`
#ASSERT `the gap in` (`the year` 2026 `in` `Quebec` `aged` 34 `with` `Priya's income` `spouse` `no spouse` `dependant` `no eligible dependant` `disability` `no disability` `withheld` 0 `OAS withheld` 0 `instalments` 0) EQUALS JUST `an individual resident in Quebec at the end of the year has the s 120(2) abatement, which is not encoded`
#ASSERT `the return for the year` (`the year` 2025 `in` `another province or territory` `aged` 34 `with` `Priya's income` `spouse` `no spouse` `dependant` `no eligible dependant` `disability` `no disability` `withheld` 0 `OAS withheld` 0 `instalments` 0) `plain CWB facts` EQUALS `not covered` `the indexed amounts of a taxation year other than 2026 are not deposited`

-- s 118(1.1): E is nil up to 181,440; at 219,961 it is (219,961 - 181,440) / (258,482 - 181,440) = 38,521 / 77,042 = 1/2,
-- so 14,829 + 1,623 x 1/2 = 15,640.50; at 258,482 or more, 14,829.
#ASSERT `the basic personal amount for` 100000 `with` `the 2026 amounts` EQUALS 16452
#ASSERT `the basic personal amount for` 219961 `with` `the 2026 amounts` EQUALS 15640.5
#ASSERT `the basic personal amount for` 300000 `with` `the 2026 amounts` EQUALS 14829

-- s 118(1)(a): a supported spouse with $5,000 of income: 16,452 + (0 + 16,452 - 5,000) = 27,904; with $20,000, the
-- second part is nil (s 257) and the amount is 16,452.
#ASSERT `the s 118(1) status amount` `the 2026 amounts` 50000 (`a spouse with income` 5000 `DTC` FALSE) `no eligible dependant` EQUALS 27904
#ASSERT `the s 118(1) status amount` `the 2026 amounts` 50000 (`a spouse with income` 20000 `DTC` FALSE) `no eligible dependant` EQUALS 16452

-- s 118(2): the age amount is nil above 46,432 + 9,208 / 15% = 107,818.67; nil under 65.
#ASSERT `the s 118(2) age amount` `the 2026 amounts` 70 120000 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the s 118(2) age amount` `the 2026 amounts` 64 20000 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the s 118(2) age amount` `the 2026 amounts` 65 40000 EQUALS 9208

-- s 118(7): under 65, RRIF payments are not qualified pension income unless received because of a spouse's death.
#ASSERT `the eligible pension income` 60 (`income of employment` 0 `less s 8` 0 `OAS` 0 `GIS` 0 `CPP` 0 `annuity` 10000 `other pension` 5000 `EI` 0 `social assistance` 0 `property` 0 `business` 0 `RRSP` 0 `limit` 0 `enhanced CPP` 0 `base CPP` 0 `EI premiums` 0) EQUALS 10000

-- s 118.3(1): an adult, 10,341; a child of 10 with $4,000 of care costs: 10,341 + (6,032 - (4,000 - 3,533 = 467)) = 15,906.
#ASSERT `the s 118.3(1) disability amount` `the 2026 amounts` 40 (`a disability certificate with care costs` 0) EQUALS 10341
#ASSERT `the s 118.3(1) disability amount` `the 2026 amounts` 10 (`a disability certificate with care costs` 4000) EQUALS 15906
#ASSERT `the s 118.3(1) disability amount` `the 2026 amounts` 40 `no disability` EQUALS 0

-- s 118(11): credits of 9,800 (a base of 70,000 at 14%): 7.14% x (9,800 - 8,193.22 = 1,606.78) = 114.724092.
#ASSERT `the s 118(11) top-up credit` `the 2026 amounts` 9800 EQUALS 114.724092
#ASSERT `the s 118(11) top-up credit` `the 2026 amounts` 5000 EQUALS 0

