-- taxable income 12,900.
#ASSERT `the taxable income` `the 2026 amounts` (`income of employment` 0 `less s 8` 0 `OAS` 8900 `GIS` 6000 `CPP` 4000 `annuity` 0 `other pension` 0 `EI` 0 `social assistance` 0 `property` 0 `business` 0 `RRSP` 0 `limit` 0 `enhanced CPP` 0 `base CPP` 0 `EI premiums` 0) EQUALS 12900

-- s 3(d): a business loss of 10,000 against 25,000 of EI benefits: income 15,000.
#ASSERT `the income for the year` `the 2026 amounts` (`income of employment` 0 `less s 8` 0 `OAS` 0 `GIS` 0 `CPP` 0 `annuity` 0 `other pension` 0 `EI` 25000 `social assistance` 0 `property` 0 `business` -10000 `RRSP` 0 `limit` 0 `enhanced CPP` 0 `base CPP` 0 `EI premiums` 0) EQUALS 15000

-- s 117(2) at the top: 300,000: 8,193.22 + 20.5% x 58,522 + 26% x 64,395 + 29% x 77,042 + 33% x 41,518
-- = 8,193.22 + 11,997.01 + 16,742.70 + 22,342.18 + 13,700.94 = 72,976.05.
