§ `The Canada workers benefit, one rule at a time`

-- Single, working income 20,000, income 30,000 (10,000 of interest): A = lesser of 1,665 and 27% x 17,000 = 4,590, so
-- 1,665; B = 15% x (30,000 - 27,392) = 391.20; CWB 1,273.80.
`a single worker` MEANS `the year` 2026 `in` `another province or territory` `aged` 40 `with` (`income of employment` 20000 `less s 8` 0 `OAS` 0 `GIS` 0 `CPP` 0 `annuity` 0 `other pension` 0 `EI` 0 `social assistance` 0 `property` 10000 `business` 0 `RRSP` 0 `limit` 0 `enhanced CPP` 0 `base CPP` 0 `EI premiums` 0) `spouse` `no spouse` `dependant` `no eligible dependant` `disability` (`a disability certificate with care costs` 0) `withheld` 0 `OAS withheld` 0 `instalments` 0
#ASSERT `the s 122.7(2) basic amount` `the 2026 amounts` `a single worker` `plain CWB facts` EQUALS 1273.8
-- The disability supplement: C = lesser of 860 and 27% x (20,000 - 1,150); D = 15% x (30,000 - 38,495), nil; 860.
#ASSERT `the Canada workers benefit for the year` `a single worker` `plain CWB facts` EQUALS `answered` (`CWB figures` WITH `basic amount` IS 1273.8, `disability supplement` IS 860, `total` IS 2133.8)
-- 18 at the end of the year, no spouse, no child: not an eligible individual.
#ASSERT NOT (`an eligible individual under s 122.7(1)` (`the year` 2026 `in` `another province or territory` `aged` 18 `with` `Priya's income` `spouse` `no spouse` `dependant` `no eligible dependant` `disability` `no disability` `withheld` 0 `OAS withheld` 0 `instalments` 0) `plain CWB facts`)
-- A full-time student for more than 13 weeks without an eligible dependant is ineligible.
#ASSERT `an ineligible individual under s 122.7(1)` `a single worker` (`CWB facts` WITH `the parent of a child with whom the individual resides` IS FALSE, `has an eligible dependant` IS FALSE, `described in s 149(1)(a) or (b)` IS FALSE, `a full-time student for more than 13 weeks` IS TRUE, `confined to a prison for 90 days or more` IS FALSE, `the individual is the one of the couple who claims` IS TRUE, `files a return of income for the year` IS TRUE)

-- s 122.7(1.3): a couple, the individual working 30,000 and the spouse 10,000 (each with that income). The individual's
-- working income is not less, so the spouse's adjusted net income is reduced by the lesser of 10,000 and 16,714, to nil.
-- Family adjusted net income 30,000. A = lesser of 2,869 and 27% x 37,000; B = 15% x (30,000 - 31,251), nil. CWB 2,869.
`a working couple` MEANS `the year` 2026 `in` `another province or territory` `aged` 40 `with` (`income of employment` 30000 `less s 8` 0 `OAS` 0 `GIS` 0 `CPP` 0 `annuity` 0 `other pension` 0 `EI` 0 `social assistance` 0 `property` 0 `business` 0 `RRSP` 0 `limit` 0 `enhanced CPP` 0 `base CPP` 0 `EI premiums` 0) `spouse` (`a spouse with income` 10000 `DTC` FALSE) `dependant` `no eligible dependant` `disability` `no disability` `withheld` 0 `OAS withheld` 0 `instalments` 0
#ASSERT `the family adjusted net income` `the 2026 amounts` `a working couple` EQUALS 30000
#ASSERT `the s 122.7(2) basic amount` `the 2026 amounts` `a working couple` `plain CWB facts` EQUALS 2869
-- If the spouse claims for the couple (s 122.7(5)), the individual gets no basic amount.
#ASSERT `the s 122.7(2) basic amount` `the 2026 amounts` `a working couple` (`CWB facts` WITH `the parent of a child with whom the individual resides` IS FALSE, `has an eligible dependant` IS FALSE, `described in s 149(1)(a) or (b)` IS FALSE, `a full-time student for more than 13 weeks` IS FALSE, `confined to a prison for 90 days or more` IS FALSE, `the individual is the one of the couple who claims` IS FALSE, `files a return of income for the year` IS TRUE) EQUALS 0

-- Alberta: a s 122.71 agreement replaces the amounts; not covered.
#ASSERT `the Canada workers benefit for the year` (`the year` 2026 `in` `Alberta` `aged` 31 `with` `Jordan's income` `spouse` `no spouse` `dependant` (`my child aged` 8) `disability` `no disability` `withheld` 0 `OAS withheld` 0 `instalments` 0) `Jordan's CWB facts` EQUALS `not covered` `the CWB of a resident of Alberta, Quebec or Nunavut is replaced under a s 122.71 agreement, which is not deposited`
-- Both spouses may deduct a disability amount and there is an eligible dependant: D(b) and D(c) both read (finding 4).
#ASSERT `the Canada workers benefit for the year` (`the year` 2026 `in` `another province or territory` `aged` 40 `with` `Jordan's income` `spouse` (`a spouse with income` 5000 `DTC` TRUE) `dependant` `no eligible dependant` `disability` (`a disability certificate with care costs` 0) `withheld` 0 `OAS withheld` 0 `instalments` 0) `Jordan's CWB facts` EQUALS `not covered` `s 122.7(3) D(b) and D(c) both apply when the spouse may deduct a disability amount and there is an eligible dependant`

§ `The Canada child benefit, one rule at a time`

-- Three children (2, 5 and 9), adjusted income 100,000: E = 8,157 x 2 + 6,883 = 23,197; Q = 8,476 + 8% x (100,000 -
-- 82,847 = 17,153) = 8,476 + 1,372.24 = 9,848.24; A = 13,348.76 a year.
#ASSERT `the Canada child benefit for the month` (`CCB for` 2027 2 `adjusted income` 100000 `children` (LIST (`a child living with me aged` 2), (`a child living with me aged` 5), (`a child living with me aged` 9))) EQUALS `answered` (13348.76 DIVIDED BY 12)
-- One child of 10 for whom the disability amount may be deducted, adjusted income 90,000: E = 6,883; Q = 3,123 + 3.2% x
-- 7,153 = 3,351.896; A = 3,531.104; N = 3,480; O = 3.2% x 7,153 = 228.896; M = 3,251.104. A + M = 6,782.208 a year.
`a child with a disability aged ten` MEANS `CCB child` WITH
    `age at the beginning of the month`               IS 10
    `resides with the individual`                     IS TRUE
    `the individual primarily fulfils the responsibility for care and upbringing` IS TRUE
    `the individual is a shared-custody parent`       IS FALSE
    `claimed as a spouse or under a special allowance` IS FALSE
    `the disability amount may be deducted for the child` IS TRUE
    `a notice has been filed for the child`           IS TRUE
#ASSERT `the Canada child benefit for the month` (`CCB for` 2026 9 `adjusted income` 90000 `children` (LIST `a child with a disability aged ten`)) EQUALS `answered` (6782.208 DIVIDED BY 12)
-- A child of 18 is not a qualified dependant: nothing.
#ASSERT `the Canada child benefit for the month` (`CCB for` 2026 9 `adjusted income` 20000 `children` (LIST (`a child living with me aged` 18))) EQUALS `answered` 0
-- A month before July 2026: not covered.
#ASSERT `the Canada child benefit for the month` (`CCB for` 2026 3 `adjusted income` 26500 `children` `Jordan's children`) EQUALS `not covered` `the CCB amounts for a month outside July 2026 to June 2027 are not deposited`
-- A shared-custody parent: not covered.
#ASSERT `the Canada child benefit for the month` (`CCB for` 2026 9 `adjusted income` 30000 `children` (LIST (`CCB child` WITH `age at the beginning of the month` IS 5, `resides with the individual` IS TRUE, `the individual primarily fulfils the responsibility for care and upbringing` IS FALSE, `the individual is a shared-custody parent` IS TRUE, `claimed as a spouse or under a special allowance` IS FALSE, `the disability amount may be deducted for the child` IS FALSE, `a notice has been filed for the child` IS TRUE))) EQUALS `not covered` `a shared-custody parent's amount under s 122.61(1.1) or s 122.5(3.06) is not encoded`

§ `The GST/HST credit, one rule at a time`

-- Single, no dependants, income 15,000: A = 445 + lesser of 234 and 2% x (15,000 - 11,564 = 3,436) = 68.72; 513.72;
-- B nil. A quarter: 128.43.
#ASSERT `the GST/HST credit for the specified month` (`GST credit for` 2026 10 `aged` 25 `qualified relation` FALSE `dependants` 0 `claims s 118(1)(b)` FALSE `income` 15000 `adjusted income` 15000) EQUALS `answered` 128.43
-- A couple, no children, adjusted income 50,000: A = 890; B = 5% x 3,568 = 178.40; a quarter of 711.60 = 177.90.
#ASSERT `the GST/HST credit for the specified month` (`GST credit for` 2027 4 `aged` 45 `qualified relation` TRUE `dependants` 0 `claims s 118(1)(b)` FALSE `income` 30000 `adjusted income` 50000) EQUALS `answered` 177.9
-- 18 and never married or a parent: not an eligible individual.
#ASSERT `the GST/HST credit for the specified month` (`GST credit for` 2026 7 `aged` 18 `qualified relation` FALSE `dependants` 0 `claims s 118(1)(b)` FALSE `income` 9000 `adjusted income` 9000) EQUALS `answered` 0
-- January 2026 falls under s 122.5(3.004), not encoded; July 2028 is indexed (s 117.1(2)(m.1)) and not covered.
#ASSERT `the GST/HST credit for the specified month` (`GST credit for` 2026 1 `aged` 40 `qualified relation` FALSE `dependants` 0 `claims s 118(1)(b)` FALSE `income` 15000 `adjusted income` 15000) EQUALS `not covered` `the GST/HST credit is encoded only for the months July 2026 to April 2028 under s 122.5(3.005)`
#ASSERT `the GST/HST credit for the specified month` (`GST credit for` 2028 7 `aged` 40 `qualified relation` FALSE `dependants` 0 `claims s 118(1)(b)` FALSE `income` 15000 `adjusted income` 15000) EQUALS `not covered` `the GST/HST credit is encoded only for the months July 2026 to April 2028 under s 122.5(3.005)`

§ `Duties`

`ordinary filing facts` MEANS `Filing facts` WITH
    `had a taxable capital gain or disposed of capital property` IS FALSE
    `has a positive HBP or LLP balance at the end of the year` IS FALSE
    `the Minister has demanded a return`               IS FALSE
    `the individual or the cohabiting spouse carried on a business` IS FALSE
    `able to file`                                     IS TRUE

`a business owner's filing facts` MEANS `Filing facts` WITH
    `had a taxable capital gain or disposed of capital property` IS FALSE
    `has a positive HBP or LLP balance at the end of the year` IS FALSE
    `the Minister has demanded a return`               IS FALSE
    `the individual or the cohabiting spouse carried on a business` IS TRUE
    `able to file`                                     IS TRUE

#ASSERT `days to the filing-due date` `ordinary filing facts` EQUALS 120
#ASSERT `days to the filing-due date` `a business owner's filing facts` EQUALS 166
#ASSERT `who files the return` FALSE EQUALS `the individual's guardian, committee or other legal representative`

-- s 150(1)(d): Priya files on day 100 (10 April 2027): fulfilled.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`the duty to file a return` TRUE `ordinary filing facts`) 0 (LIST EVENT `the individual` `file a return of income for the year` 100) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- Not required: nothing is owed even if no return is filed.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`the duty to file a return` FALSE `ordinary filing facts`) 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL 200)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- A business owner files on day 150 (30 May 2027): in time.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`the duty to file a return` TRUE `a business owner's filing facts`) 0 (LIST EVENT `the individual` `file a return of income for the year` 150) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- An employee files on day 150: late.
-- expect: BREACH by the individual, "no return of income was filed by the filing-due date (s 150(1)(d))"
#TRACE `the duty to file a return` TRUE `ordinary filing facts` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the individual` DOES `file a return of income for the year` AT 150

-- s 156.1(4): a balance of 400 paid with 500 on day 110: fulfilled. No balance: fulfilled.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`the duty to pay the balance` 400) 0 (LIST EVENT `the individual` (`pay the balance` 500) 110) EQUALS FULFILLED
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`the duty to pay the balance` -663.7773) 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL 200)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: BREACH by the individual, "the balance of tax was not paid by the balance-due day (s 156.1(4))"
#TRACE `the duty to pay the balance` 400 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the individual` DOES `pay the balance` 300 AT 100
    (WAITUNTIL 130)

-- s 156.1(2)(b): net tax owing 4,200 this year, 3,500 last year, 2,800 the year before: instalments are required. With
-- 2,900 this year, they are not; with 4,200 this year but 2,500 and 2,800 before, they are not.
#ASSERT `the net tax owing` 9000 4000 7800 1000 EQUALS 4200
#ASSERT `instalments are required` 4200 3500 2800
#ASSERT NOT (`instalments are required` 2900 3500 2800)
#ASSERT NOT (`instalments are required` 4200 2500 2800)
-- s 156(1)(a)(ii): an instalment base of 4,200 for last year: 1,050 a quarter. The first is due on 15 March, day 74.
#ASSERT `a quarter of` 4200 EQUALS 1050
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`the duty to pay instalment` 1 TRUE 1050) 0 (LIST EVENT `the individual` (`pay an instalment` 1050) 70) EQUALS FULFILLED
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`the duty to pay instalment` 4 TRUE 1050) 0 (LIST EVENT `the individual` (`pay an instalment` 1050) 340) EQUALS FULFILLED
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`the duty to pay instalment` 2 FALSE 1050) 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL 400)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: BREACH by the individual, "an instalment was not paid by its day under s 156(1)"
#TRACE `the duty to pay instalment` 1 TRUE 1050 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the individual` DOES `pay an instalment` 1050 AT 80

-- s 122.62(6): Jordan separates on 15 August 2026: notice is due by 30 September, 16 + 30 = 46 days later.
#ASSERT `days from the event to the end of the next calendar month` 15 8 2026 EQUALS 46
#ASSERT `days from the event to the end of the next calendar month` 20 12 2026 EQUALS 42
#ASSERT `days from the event to the end of the next calendar month` 10 1 2028 EQUALS 50
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`the duty to notify a change of cohabiting spouse` 46) 0 (LIST EVENT `the individual` `notify the Minister of the change` 20) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: BREACH by the individual, "the change of cohabiting spouse or common-law partner was not notified in time (s 122.62)"
#TRACE `the duty to notify a change of cohabiting spouse` 46 AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 60)
